      ":question/problem": "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨2t,\\,3\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 2 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨10u,\\,3\\sqrt{5u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=5k$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
